C3: FROBENIUS/CF reading of the {1,q} family.
   meas(G_{1,q}) = 5/7 + 1/(7q). deficit from 6/7 = (q-1)/(7q) = (1/7)(1-1/q).
   (1-1/q) = density of <1,q>-overlap; q->inf gives the pure 1/7 deficit (lonely-runner floor).
   The binding q=13 is the LARGEST q in P={1..13}: the extremal CF endpoint.
   => binding G_P = the single-partial-quotient (simplest CF) pair at max denominator.
